WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
- All right, y'all, we are back

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.770
as we continue to celebrate talented kids

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.080
all over the country.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.300
Not long ago, I had Terry Bradshaw

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.790
and Iain Armitage on the show.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.610
It was such an interesting combo.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.240
The conversation got flowing so much so

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.740
we couldn't actually
include everything we taped

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.820
in that episode.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.190
So today we're showing something

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.940
we never got to air, another
incredibly talented kid.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.371
Perfect for this hour, check it out.

00:00:23.371 --> 00:00:24.204
Welcome back, y'all,

00:00:24.204 --> 00:00:25.600
I'm here with Terry Bradshaw.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.600
Give it up.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.461
- Whoa.

00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:28.573
(audience applauding)

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:30.060
- Alright y'all, at eight years old,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.690
my next guest is well on his way

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.050
to making his mark in the world of dance.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.760
When his recital was postponed
this summer due to COVID

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.560
he decided it wasn't going to
stop him from choreographing

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.380
his and performing his special routine.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:45.540
He even let his six year old
sister join in on the act.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.078
Check it out.

00:00:47.078 --> 00:00:50.411
(mystical ballet music)

00:01:11.752 --> 00:01:13.097
Since his mom posted that video,

00:01:13.097 --> 00:01:15.730
Maximus has gained quite a following,

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.510
not just for his moves,
but for what he represents.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.720
We have Maximus on the line,
along with his mama, Michelle.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.310
How are y'all doing?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.200
- Good.
- Good, Kelly.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.100
- Hi, well Maximus and
Michelle meet Terry Bradshaw.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.530
He's over here, if y'all can see him.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:31.363
- [Terry] Hey Maximus, how ya doing bud?

00:01:31.363 --> 00:01:32.829
- [Michelle] Hey Terry,
my husband loves you.

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:33.662
- [Maximus] Hey Terry.

00:01:33.662 --> 00:01:35.810
- Oh thank you, I would
have fallen down three

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:39.230
or four times watching that,
if I'd been doing that.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:41.000
- He was watching you dance Maximus

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.320
and goes I'd of fallen
down a few times already.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.020
Well, Maximus you've got moves.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.813
So how did you get into dance?

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:51.410
- So it first started when I was two and I

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.360
did non-stop dancing around the house.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.193
So at three years old, I
did my first dance class.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.440
And so I love dance.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.200
It makes me so happy.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.200
I do jazz, ballet, tap, hip hop,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.003
acro, baton, and color
guard, that's my art.

00:02:13.003 --> 00:02:14.603
- Wow.
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:17.184 --> 00:02:19.090
- And my favorite type of dance is ballet.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.682
- Oh my God.

00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:22.030
You are so graceful, pointing that toe.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.930
I was like, oh, my toes started cramping.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.830
I was like, I can't do it.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.033
Well Maximus, tell us about
this recital performance.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.541
- So our recital got postponed

00:02:32.541 --> 00:02:36.250
because we had to move and
we're going to miss it.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.540
So I decided to make up my own recital

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.390
with my sister included in it.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:47.390
And it took us almost a month
to like, get it correct.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:53.340
And so we did songs from
Beethoven, Chopin, and Tchaikovsky.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.813
- Oh my God.
- Very good.

00:02:56.813 --> 00:02:58.513
- [Kelly] The fact that
you know those names.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.457
- Can you spell them?
- It was.

00:03:02.736 --> 00:03:05.560
- And beautiful Mom here helped

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.590
with my sister's hair and costume.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.750
- [Kelly] Aww, that's awesome.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:10.640
It's a family event.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.473
I love it.

00:03:11.473 --> 00:03:13.020
Did you ever try dance or gymnastics?

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:13.920
- Square dance.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.240
- Square dancing, you're so Southern.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.090
Well, I hear a lot of football players,

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.260
don't they do ballet sometimes?

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.700
- [Terry] Now, did the line dancing with,

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.075
when it came out in the '70's.

00:03:24.075 --> 00:03:24.908
- [Kelly] Wait line, dancing?

00:03:24.908 --> 00:03:26.713
like line dancing, like at
a cowboy bar, or like, a?

00:03:26.713 --> 00:03:27.800
- [Terry] Yes, yes.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.950
- Oh yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.023
- [Terry] Yeah, but
that's it, I'm no dancer.

00:03:33.193 --> 00:03:34.159
- Okay.
- I guess to sum it up.

00:03:34.159 --> 00:03:35.419
- [Kelly] There's another show.

00:03:35.419 --> 00:03:37.470
I want to see you on that.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.010
Well, Michelle, you say Maximus
has had to deal with a lot

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.683
of different reactions as
a black male dancer, right?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.480
- [Michelle] Yes, we're a military family

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.880
and Maximus has lived in
five different places.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.160
And he's also been to five
different dance studios.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.070
And most dancers are white females.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.570
And Maximus is obviously neither of those.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:58.140
So often when he goes
to a new dance studio

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.920
he'll come home sad because he says,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.512
no one talked to, talks to him.

00:04:02.512 --> 00:04:03.980
And he sits in the corner by himself.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.040
But then once Maximums finally does

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.770
some different dance moves and
people see that he's actually

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:11.260
just as passionate
about dance as they are,

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.144
then they embrace him and
then he becomes friends.

00:04:14.144 --> 00:04:15.480
- [Kelly] Look at him.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.863
You get it, Maximus.

00:04:18.119 --> 00:04:19.410
- This is our house all day, every day.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.840
- I swear to God, if I could do that,

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.890
I'd be doing it right now.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.570
- [Terry] If you could do that,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.542
that's exactly how they'd
take you to the hospital.

00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:29.486
(Terry and Kelly laughing)

00:04:29.486 --> 00:04:30.353
- [Kelly] I'd be like stuck.

00:04:30.353 --> 00:04:31.820
It'd be fine.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.410
Well Maximus, you say you
want to be a role model

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.363
to other young dancers, right?

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.017
- Definitely, so one
time somebody was like,

00:04:41.017 --> 00:04:42.290
"Oh, boys don't dance."

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.040
And I was like, yes, they do.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.650
And so I think that all boys should dance,

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.155
including you, Terry.

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:52.480
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.680
- Hey, I'm gonna tell you what.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.120
My son, my four year old son, he loves,

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.390
he and my daughter

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:59.407
both listen to this giant music
box thing I have at my house

00:04:59.407 --> 00:05:01.806
and they turn it on and they took,

00:05:01.806 --> 00:05:03.930
and they both put on ballet
recitals all, every day.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:06.520
Like they love, they both
love ballet, my son loves it.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.010
He loves doing it just as much as River.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.390
I think it's awesome.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:11.950
And it's beautiful.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.995
So Maximus, I know that you
have a number of celebrity fans.

00:05:15.995 --> 00:05:18.630
Well we happen to have one on the line

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.880
who wants to meet you.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.990
He's a young performer
and he's even giving you,

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.380
he's giving you a shout
out on social media.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.893
So say hi to Young Sheldon
himself, Iain Armitage.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.040
- Hey Maximus.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.010
- Hi.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:35.510
- Oh my gosh, y'all are so cool.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:38.663
So Iain, what would you like
to say anything to Maximus?

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:44.850
- Yes, you are amazing, oh my goodness.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:47.310
When I watched the dance
recital you did with your sister

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.150
I was like, okay, this kid is incredible.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:52.120
Then I read up on you some more.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.830
You are like amazing.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.580
They said, do you have any like

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.210
words that you would
want to say to Maximus?

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.960
Like as inspiration or something?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.240
I said, I think he should be
saying inspirational words

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:06.160
to me because this kid is awesome.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.561
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:06:07.561 --> 00:06:08.394
- You are destined to great things.

00:06:08.394 --> 00:06:10.030
You are the coolest, thank you so much

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:13.470
for being a wonderful
role model for everyone.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.180
And yes, boys do dance

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.120
and I think it's wonderful what you do.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.610
You're graceful, you're amazing.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.500
You're strong, you're awesome.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.250
Don't let anyone tell you otherwise

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.050
- [Kelly] Iain Armitage for president.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.620
- Yes that was so well said.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.610
- [Kelly] I love you Iain.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:30.620
Maximus, we do love you.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:31.453
I loved your moves.

00:06:31.453 --> 00:06:33.210
I think it was very inspiring
and it was beautiful.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.770
It was graceful on you,
I love your moves, man.

